# Code owners for se-client-kit. GitHub requests a review from the owners of
# every changed path, and branch protection can require their approval.
# The last matching pattern wins.
#
# TODO: name the owners. The decision for this public repository is that the two
# organization owners are the code owners, and an author never approves their own
# change. Add the real GitHub handles here once the owners provide them; do not
# guess them. Until then no rule is active, so no review is auto-requested.
#
# Intended shape once the handles are known (replace <owner-1> and <owner-2>):
#
#   *                         @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#
# Paths that can reach the supply chain or a credential should never be left to
# the default silently. List them explicitly even when the owners are the same:
#
#   /.github/                 @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#   /.ai/                     @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#   /.claude/                 @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#   /.opencode/               @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#   /.agents/                 @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#   /AGENTS.md                @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#   /CLAUDE.md                @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#   /package.json             @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#   /pnpm-lock.yaml           @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#   /pnpm-workspace.yaml      @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#   /.npmrc                   @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#   /.node-version            @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#   /packages/contracts/      @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#   /specs/                   @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#   /decisions/               @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#   /runbook/                 @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
#   /SECURITY.md              @<owner-1> @<owner-2>
